Having spent a relatively large amount of time trying to compile Nethack
using djgcc, I have a couple of pointers.

1)  The nethack code is written in traditional C.  Borland C won't like
it unless it has a -traditional mode.  To fix it, you will have to
convert the function declarations from
void func(a)
    XCHAR a;
{blah}
to
void func( XCHAR a)
{blah}
Kind of a pain, but worth it (saves on data size!).

2)  I don't know about Borland C, but C on MS-DOS generally handles
signals poorly/not-at-all, so #define NOSIGNAL (or NO_SIGNAL or whatever
it says in the code).

Doing both of those things should get everything but zap.c and msdos.c
compiled.  I'm STILL trying to get them to work.  Good Luck!


